    "source_round_trip": [
      "For each version, set version and ref from hosted_source.references. Run this command from the source repository to capture the reference archive.",
      "python3 -B -c 'import json, subprocess, sys; commit, version, ref = sys.argv[1:]; path = f\"verification/identity-network-current-source-v{version}/selected-source-manifest.json\"; roster = json.loads(subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{commit}:{path}\"])); subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-c\", \"tar.umask=0022\", \"archive\", \"--format=tar\", ref, \"--\", *roster], check=True)' \"$commit\" \"$version\" \"$ref\" > \"$scratch/v$version.tar\"",
      "Use git ls-tree -rz on each ref to check the listed modes and blob OIDs. For 65 to 64 and 64 to 63, reverse each selection exact_delta using the Git bytes and modes under its preimages directory and remove rows with null before. Reapply the after blobs and modes from the newer ref. Compare all path/mode/bytes tuples in both directions to the tar references.",
      "Compare each ordinary or opt-in migration directory with git ls-tree -rz on versions 64 and 65. The ordinary roster also matches hosted/test/support/reviewed_migrations.json."
    ],
    "sparse_projection": [
      "For each projections entry, use its key for job and its workflow field for workflow. Set repo to a fresh directory and execute the following.",
      "git -C \"$repo\" -c init.templateDir= init -q",
      "git -C \"$repo\" config core.hooksPath /dev/null",
      "git -C \"$repo\" config core.autocrlf false",
      "git -C \"$repo\" config core.filemode true",
      "printf \"%s\\n\" \"$objects\" > \"$repo/.git/objects/info/alternates\"",
      "git -C \"$source_repo\" show \"$commit:.github/workflows/$workflow.yml\" | awk -v job=\"$job\" '$0 == \"  \" job \":\" { found=1; next } found && $0 == \"          sparse-checkout: |\" { block=1; next } block && /^            / { print substr($0, 13); next } block { exit }' > \"$scratch/$job.rules\"",
      "git -C \"$repo\" sparse-checkout set --no-cone --stdin < \"$scratch/$job.rules\"",
      "git -C \"$repo\" checkout --detach \"$commit\"",
      "git -C \"$repo\" ls-tree -rz --name-only \"$commit\" | git -C \"$repo\" sparse-checkout check-rules -z > \"$scratch/$job.paths\"",
